# Unambiguous dashboard answer approval
Workstream-ID: lea-25
GitHub-Issue: https://github.com/Zanark/LinkedIn-EasyApply-Automaton/issues/25
Publication: PUBLIC_SAFE_PROJECTION
Source-record: Reviewed bounded dashboard correction-review improvement
Status: DONE
Milestone: Make the exact answer selected for saving obvious
Dependencies: lea-09

## Purpose
Make the editable answer and its selection an obvious pair in the resume
correction table. Distinguish the saved value from the previous answer and
resume reference without changing question identity or override precedence.

## Tasks
- [x] Inspect the existing editor and capture the prior source/tracking baseline.
- [x] Group the editable value with its selection and explain the read-only references.
- [x] Cover the presentation and selected-value persistence with fictional checks.
- [x] Verify ordinary editing, selection and saving in an isolated browser.
- [x] Update affected guides and reconcile scoped tracking.

## Acceptance criteria
- [x] The editable answer is adjacent to its clearly named save checkbox.
- [x] Reference answers are explicitly read-only and cannot be mistaken for the save target.
- [x] Saving affects only selected nonempty values, retaining question identity and precedence.
- [x] Native content sizing, manual resizing and narrow-view scrolling remain available.
- [x] Qualification uses fictional data without driving independent user applications.
- [x] Prior Reports/autosizing work, private inputs, older workstreams and releases are preserved.
- [x] One repository issue, one correctly staged Project item and a durable backlink represent the workstream.

## Completion evidence
The table pairs Answer to save with Save this answer immediately after the
question. Previous answer and Resume reference are explicitly read-only.
Prominent instructions, two-line purpose/example help, a selected count and
Save selected answers identify exactly which values will be saved. Internal
editor keys, the original persistence loop and override precedence are retained.

Black, Ruff and scoped mypy pass; all sixteen focused cases pass. New checks
cover presentation, initial disabled saving, selected edited values, trimming,
empty selected values and untouched unchecked rows. The presentation regression
reproduced the previous column order before the change.

Six isolated real-browser boundaries pass using ordinary native gestures:
headers/read-only references, dragging/Autosize and reload defaults, contained
narrow scrolling, editing versus explicit selection, final-value-only saving
and persisted reload. Ten successful backend completions were observed; both
layout screenshots were reviewed. The saved fictional value differs from both
references; original history, an existing override and unrelated data remain.

Five affected guides and the database method's obsolete button-label docstring
are updated. Exact full-file reconstruction preserves all prior dashboard code
outside the target renderer and all earlier table tests. Only the identified
fictional fixture was stopped and its database removed. This is bounded local
technical completion, not human acceptance, live qualification or publication.

